wpa_supplicant compares the beacon RSN IE (as cached from the on-air
frame) against the AP's echo in M3 byte-exact.  On BCM43602 with
Broadcom fw v7.35.177.61, the fw's beacon parser auto-expands the
stored RSN IE with an implicit PMKID count + group_mgmt suffix when
MFPC is set in RSN capabilities.  Beacon-cache ends up 32 bytes;
M3 arrives verbatim from hostapd at 26 bytes; byte-exact compare
fires WLAN_REASON_IE_IN_4WAY_DIFFERS (reason=17) locally-generated,
and the 4-way handshake tears down right after the IGTK material
has been received (i.e., at the last mile of full MFP bring-up).

Add a semantic fallback in wpa_compare_rsn_ie: after the byte-exact
try, parse both IEs and accept the mismatch if proto, pairwise
cipher, group cipher, key_mgmt bitfield, RSN capabilities, and
mgmt_group_cipher all agree.  The parser defaults mgmt_group_cipher
to AES-128-CMAC when the suffix is absent, matching what the
explicit suffix advertises, so the shortened IE ends up equivalent.

Apply on target (FreeBSD 15.1 base tree):
    sudo patch -p0 -d/ < wpa_supplicant-semantic-rsn-ie-compare.diff
    cd /usr/src/usr.sbin/wpa && sudo make -j4
    sudo install -o root -g wheel -m 555 \
        /usr/obj/usr/src/$(uname -m).$(uname -m)/usr.sbin/wpa/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant \
        /usr/local/sbin/wpa_supplicant

Verified live-fire on fbsdmac BCM43602 against Ubuntu hostapd v2.10
in MFP-optional mode:
    wpa_state=COMPLETED at t=2 s
    key_mgmt=WPA2-PSK-SHA256   pmf=1
    DHCPACK from 10.99.0.1, bound to 10.99.0.17
    3/3 pings 1.5-8.7 ms
    dmesg: fmop_set_key: IGTK idx=4 algo=4 rc=0

--- /usr/src/contrib/wpa/src/common/wpa_common.c.orig
+++ /usr/src/contrib/wpa/src/common/wpa_common.c
@@ -2868,6 +2868,29 @@
 	if (ie1len == ie2len && os_memcmp(ie1, ie2, ie1len) == 0)
 		return 0; /* identical IEs */

+	{
+		/*
+		 * Semantic-compare fallback: some fw beacon caches auto-
+		 * expand the parsed RSN IE with an implicit PMKID count +
+		 * group_mgmt suffix when MFPC is set in RSN caps.  A
+		 * strict byte-compare against the AP's echo in M3 then
+		 * mismatches even though the fields agree.  Accept the
+		 * mismatch if every parsed field is equivalent; the
+		 * parser defaults mgmt_group_cipher to AES-128-CMAC when
+		 * the suffix is absent, matching what the explicit suffix
+		 * would advertise.
+		 */
+		struct wpa_ie_data ie1d, ie2d;
+		if (wpa_parse_wpa_ie_rsn(ie1, ie1len, &ie1d) == 0 &&
+		    wpa_parse_wpa_ie_rsn(ie2, ie2len, &ie2d) == 0 &&
+		    ie1d.proto == ie2d.proto &&
+		    ie1d.pairwise_cipher == ie2d.pairwise_cipher &&
+		    ie1d.group_cipher == ie2d.group_cipher &&
+		    ie1d.key_mgmt == ie2d.key_mgmt &&
+		    ie1d.capabilities == ie2d.capabilities &&
+		    ie1d.mgmt_group_cipher == ie2d.mgmt_group_cipher)
+			return 0;
+	}
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211R
 	if (ft_initial_assoc) {
 		struct wpa_ie_data ie1d, ie2d;
